WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:03.340 --> 00:00:08.010
Game show contestants have to overcome a lot
in order to emerge from the experience unscathed.

00:00:08.010 --> 00:00:12.510
There's money at stake, pressure to win, and
just the general stress of being on television

00:00:12.510 --> 00:00:16.680
for what's probably the first and only time
in their lives. It's not surprising, in other

00:00:16.680 --> 00:00:20.860
words, when the stress makes them screw up
big time. Thankfully, the internet grants

00:00:20.860 --> 00:00:24.279
these moments immortality, and we found some
of the best ones.

00:00:24.279 --> 00:00:26.619
The worst Wheel of Fortune contestant ever

00:00:26.619 --> 00:00:32.009
Indiana University honors student Julian Batts,
also known as the worst Wheel of Fortune contestant

00:00:32.009 --> 00:00:36.800
ever, put in an epically awful performance
on the show that found him offering not one,

00:00:36.800 --> 00:00:40.380
not two, but three forehead-slapping answers.

00:00:42.920 --> 00:00:46.320
First, he flubbed the pronunciation of "Achilles."

00:00:46.329 --> 00:00:50.129
"Mythological hero Achilles"

00:00:51.260 --> 00:00:51.760
(buzzer)

00:00:51.960 --> 00:00:56.329
Fair enough—let's just assume he never studied
Greek mythology and he isn't a Brad Pitt fan.

00:00:56.329 --> 00:00:59.749
Next, he blew an incredibly easy chance to win a car.

00:01:00.320 --> 00:01:00.820
"C!"

00:01:02.260 --> 00:01:02.840
(buzzer)

00:01:03.180 --> 00:01:04.420
"Can I solve?"

00:01:04.420 --> 00:01:04.920
"Ya"

00:01:04.920 --> 00:01:06.320
"The World's Fastest Man"

00:01:06.320 --> 00:01:07.420
"Ya that's it"

00:01:08.000 --> 00:01:09.959
But his guess on this puzzle...

00:01:09.959 --> 00:01:12.159
...was this:

00:01:12.159 --> 00:01:15.539
"On the spot dicespin"

00:01:15.539 --> 00:01:17.259
(buzzer)

00:01:17.259 --> 00:01:22.479
This guy thinks "dice spin" is one word—and
he also thinks you spin dice.

00:01:22.479 --> 00:01:27.139
Needless to say, it was not Indiana University's
finest moment in the spotlight.

00:01:27.139 --> 00:01:28.740
Another Wheel of Misfortune

00:01:28.740 --> 00:01:32.049
Okay, you've got three letters remaining in
this puzzle…

00:01:32.049 --> 00:01:36.529
You're probably gonna solve, right? Well,
that wasn't contestant Casey's plan. Instead

00:01:36.529 --> 00:01:39.369
she made an on the spot dicespin.

00:01:39.369 --> 00:01:43.579
Every hardcore Wheel-watcher knows she's playing
with fire, but she lucks out.

00:01:43.579 --> 00:01:49.349
After guessing the 'G' in "nightclub," she
gets to pick up the $10,000. But then when

00:01:49.349 --> 00:01:55.189
most sane people would have solved the puzzle—which
only had two letters left, Casey goes and

00:01:55.189 --> 00:01:56.469
does this:

00:01:56.469 --> 00:01:58.389
"Waddaya wanna do?"

00:01:58.389 --> 00:01:59.029
"Spin!"

00:01:59.029 --> 00:02:00.309
"Oh ok!"

00:02:00.309 --> 00:02:05.249
Casey is playing the game show equivalent
of Russian Roulette at this point. The wheel

00:02:05.249 --> 00:02:10.170
barely makes it one peg past Bankrupt. This
is complete insanity. All she has to do to

00:02:10.170 --> 00:02:16.150
get that money is say "X" or "V"--you know,
the only letters left in the word "Exclusive."

00:02:16.150 --> 00:02:18.629
"A letter?"

00:02:18.629 --> 00:02:21.110
"A K"

00:02:21.110 --> 00:02:23.590
(audience gasps)

00:02:24.860 --> 00:02:26.920
No, Casey. Just no.

00:02:26.920 --> 00:02:28.140
Romantic Geometry

00:02:28.140 --> 00:02:33.140
Jeopardy! has always leaned towards the brainier
side of televised game shows. It takes itself

00:02:33.140 --> 00:02:37.489
seriously—well, at least more seriously
than some of the competition.

00:02:37.489 --> 00:02:39.149
"Fart in the bed"

00:02:41.409 --> 00:02:45.879
That's why it was so surprising when contestant
Kara had this response to the clue:

00:02:45.879 --> 00:02:52.129
"If Andy yearns for Brenda and Brenda cares
about Charlene who pines for Andy, the 3 of

00:02:52.129 --> 00:02:53.680
them form one of these"

00:02:53.680 --> 00:02:54.290
"Kara"

00:02:54.290 --> 00:02:56.280
"What is a threesome?"

00:02:56.280 --> 00:03:01.859
To be fair her answer isn't necessarily wrong.
But it isn't necessarily right, either. The

00:03:01.859 --> 00:03:04.010
answer, of course, was "Love Triangle."

00:03:04.010 --> 00:03:07.840
Host Alex Trebek, a seasoned pro, went in
for the kill.

00:03:07.840 --> 00:03:13.079
"Kara has obviously had much more experience
than I"

00:03:13.079 --> 00:03:15.579
Trebek, you old scoundrel.

00:03:15.579 --> 00:03:16.640
Listening Helps

00:03:16.640 --> 00:03:21.040
Family Feud contestant Holly just wanted to
win the faceoff to give her family the chance

00:03:21.040 --> 00:03:25.510
to pass or play. So she didn't even let host
Steve Harvey finish the question:

00:03:25.510 --> 00:03:29.299
"Name something a woman does for her baby,
that she-"

00:03:29.299 --> 00:03:29.900
"Yes"

00:03:29.900 --> 00:03:31.680
"Changes its diaper"

00:03:31.680 --> 00:03:33.700
Bad move, Holly.

00:03:33.700 --> 00:03:34.530
(buzzer)

00:03:34.530 --> 00:03:37.980
She probably should've let Steve finish reading
his card.

00:03:37.980 --> 00:03:44.980
"Name something a woman does for her baby
that she also does for her hubby."

00:03:44.980 --> 00:03:49.469
On the other hand, maybe she and her husband
have an understanding! Who are we to judge?

00:03:49.469 --> 00:03:51.030
You do you, Holly.

00:03:51.030 --> 00:03:53.170
Some couples are truly made for each other

00:03:53.170 --> 00:03:57.529
The Newlywed Game hangs its entire premise
on the uncomfortable reality that couples

00:03:57.529 --> 00:04:02.329
may not know each other as well as they think
they do. In Gloria and Joe's case, this couldn't

00:04:02.329 --> 00:04:05.369
be further from the truth. When asked:

00:04:05.369 --> 00:04:08.449
"How many decades will your husband say his mother has lived?"

00:04:09.319 --> 00:04:14.760
Gloria visibly realizes the trouble her husband,
Joe, would have with this answer, and yet,

00:04:14.760 --> 00:04:16.300
she confidently states:

00:04:16.340 --> 00:04:18.340
"Ten decades"

00:04:20.400 --> 00:04:24.889
The audience laughs and thinks this is ridiculous,
but then Joe comes back out and we see that

00:04:24.889 --> 00:04:28.089
Gloria knows her husband better than he knows
himself:

00:04:28.480 --> 00:04:38.340
"Oh I dunno what a decade is. 44th Birthday so she'd be, that's 4 years a decade. She'd be 10 decades. 10 decades."

00:04:39.860 --> 00:04:44.920
Joe, hold onto Gloria and never let her go.
You will never find a woman who understands

00:04:44.930 --> 00:04:47.050
and accepts you like she does.

00:04:47.050 --> 00:04:51.020
Thanks for watching! Subscribe to our YouTube
channel to watch more videos like the one

00:04:51.020 --> 00:04:55.610
you just saw. And leave us a comment to let
us know which game show fails you think should've

00:04:55.610 --> 00:04:56.310
made the list...

